= Lesson 4

== Pure Dirichlet Problems

Find $u^h(x) in scr(S)^h subset scr(S) = { u | u^h(0) = u_0, u^h(L) = u_g}$ 

$=> scr(S)^h = {u^h in H^1(Omega) | u^h(0) = u_0, u^h(L) = u_g}$

such that $forall w^h in scr(V)^h in scr(V) = {w | w(0) = 0, w(L) = 0}$

$ => scr(V)^h = {w^h in H^1(Omega) | w^h(0) = 0, w^h(L) = 0}$

$integral_Omega w^h_(,x) sigma^h A d x = integral_Omega w^h f A d x$

Basis functions: linear polynomials over $Omega^e$

$w^h_(e=1) = N^2(xi)c^2_(e=1), w^h_(e=n_"el") = N^1(xi)c^1_(e=n_"el")$

$integral_Omega w^h_(,x) sigma^h A d x = c_1^2 (E A)/h^e mat(-1, 1) mat(d_1^1; d^2_1) + sum_(e=2)^(n_"el") mat(c^1_e, c^2_e) (E A)/h^e mat(1, -1; -1, 1) mat(d^1_e; d^2_e) + c^1_(n_"el") (E A)/h^e mat(1, -1) mat(d^1_(n_"el"); d^2_(n_"el"))$

$integral_Omega w^h f A d x = c^2_1 f A h^e/2 + sum_(e=2)^(n_"el" - 1) mat(c^1_e, c^2_e) f A h^e/2 mat(1; 1) + c^1_(n_"el") (f A h^2)/2$

